FQN: Example: Store typed values in memory and read them back
Kind: verified_example
Provenance: authored
Verification: passed
Authored example: written for foss-mcp against the pinned library, not taken from the upstream README; published only after the ingestion verifier compiled or ran it against that commit.
Writes a text, an integer, a decimal and a boolean into a new workbook, serialises it to XLSX bytes, loads the bytes back and checks each cell's stored type and value without touching the disk.

Example:
// Authored example: write text, number and boolean values into a new workbook and read them back from memory.
use aspose_cells_foss_rust::{CellValueType, Workbook};
use std::error::Error;

fn main() -> Result<(), Box<dyn Error>> {
    let mut workbook = Workbook::new();
    {
        let mut worksheets = workbook.get_worksheets_mut();
        let sheet = worksheets.get(0)?;
        let mut cells = sheet.get_cells_mut();
        cells.get("A1")?.put_value_string("Widgets")?;
        cells.get("B1")?.put_value_i32(42)?;
        cells.get("C1")?.put_value_decimal(19.99)?;
        cells.get("D1")?.put_value_bool(true)?;
    }

    // Serialise the workbook to XLSX bytes and load those bytes back; nothing touches the disk.
    let bytes = workbook.save_xlsx_to_bytes()?;
    let loaded = Workbook::load_xlsx_from_bytes(&bytes)?;
    let sheet = loaded.worksheet("Sheet1")?;
    let cells = sheet.get_cells();

    for address in ["A1", "B1", "C1", "D1"] {
        let cell = cells.get(address)?;
        println!("{} {:?} {}", address, cell.value_type(), cell.display_string_value());
    }

    assert_eq!(cells.get("A1")?.string_value(), Some("Widgets"));
    assert_eq!(cells.get("B1")?.int_value(), Some(42));
    assert_eq!(cells.get("D1")?.bool_value(), Some(true));
    assert_eq!(cells.get("C1")?.value_type(), CellValueType::IsNumeric);
    Ok(())
}
